From caa77cd7660e07ded2deec71c1fdde942086039d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 01:02:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Ship yay and the base-devel toolchain in the guest

Upstream Omarchy's AUR entry points (omarchy-pkg-aur-add, omarchy-pkg-aur-install,
omarchy-update-aur-pkgs) hard-code yay, and the trimmed factory transaction
never included it or base-devel, so a stock-looking desktop failed with
'yay: command not found' and had no 'which' either. Pull yay from the Omarchy
repository the guest already trusts, the same source upstream's own package
list uses, and add base-devel so AUR builds have their toolchain.
---
 guest/packages.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/guest/packages.txt b/guest/packages.txt
index 8fda564..fce0715 100644
--- a/guest/packages.txt
+++ b/guest/packages.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # x86_64 transaction for the real Quattro first-boot owner-provisioning flow.
 archlinux-keyring
 base
+base-devel
 bash-completion
 bat
 btop
@@ -77,6 +78,7 @@ xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
 xdg-user-dirs
 xdg-utils
 xorg-xwayland
+yay
 zoxide
 zram-generator
 zstd
-- 
2.55.0

